WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.340
Heads up, folks, major Avengers: Infinity
War spoilers coming your way.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:05.720
"I'll listen to you...

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:07.880
til this is empty."

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:13.120
The supersized Marvel blockbuster dished out
very little mercy in its heartbreaking ending

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.740
that saw big-name heroes bite the dust, literally.

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:20.570
While some characters' fates were seemingly
sealed, others were left up for interpretation,

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:23.580
like Valkyrie and the Asgardians, who didn't
appear in the film.

00:00:23.849 --> 00:00:28.820
Now, Infinity War co-director Joe Russo has
revealed what happened to Tessa Thompson's

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.760
hard-drinking Valkyrie and the rest of the
Asgardian refugees.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:37.110
That is, unless you choose to take Thompson's
word that she was in fact in the film as,

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:38.880
well, a baby goat.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:44.130
For a refresher, Infinity War picks up where
Thor: Ragnarok left off, with the tense scene

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:49.570
aboard the Grandmaster's refugee vessel that
carried Thor, Loki, Hulk, Heimdall, Valkyrie,

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.680
and the rest of the rescued citizens of Asgard.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:56.240
Thanos and his Black Order battered Thor in
an attempt to extract the Space Stone from

00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:01.300
the Tesseract, then stabbed Heimdall through
the chest, intercepted Hulk, and offed Loki.

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:06.020
Infinity War then carried on directly after
Loki took his last breath, not bothering to

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:07.920
address Valkyrie and the remaining Asgardians.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:13.400
During a Q&amp;A at his old high school in Iowa
City, Joe Russo confirmed that Valkyrie survived

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:14.760
Thanos' surprise attack.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:18.920
A student who attended Russo's presentation
took to Reddit to relay the information.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:21.740
The user wrote: "He did confirm that Valkyrie
lived."

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:26.080
Russo didn't reveal exactly how the heroine
made it out alive, but given that he mentioned

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:30.560
a portion of the Asgardians on the ship had
fled using "escape pods," it's safe to assume

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.420
that Valkyrie may have done the same.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:36.960
Though ducking away from a major battle doesn't
quite seem like something Valkyrie would do,

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:41.020
perhaps she was tasked with ensuring the last
Asgardians evacuated safely.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:45.670
Sadly, those wondering what happened to Korg,
the adorable Kronan warrior voiced by Thor:

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:49.700
Ragnarok director Taika Waititi, won't be
as pleased with Russo's remarks.

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:53.460
"I'm made of rocks, as you can see, but don't
let that intimidate you.

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:55.890
You don't need to be afraid unless you're
made of scissors.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:56.420
Heh heh.

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:58.780
Just a little rock-paper-scissors joke for
ya."

00:01:58.789 --> 00:02:03.460
The same Reddit user indicated that they asked
Russo whether Korg survived the ambush, but

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:07.810
the filmmaker answered that he wasn't, quote,
"willing to say what his fate was," at least

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:08.800
not at this time.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:12.560
So there you have it, Marvel fans: A bunch
of our precious heroes may be gone for good,

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.640
but Valkyrie is definitely still alive.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.180
Silver linings, right?

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:17.780
Thanks for watching!

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:19.970
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:22.120
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

